\name{cellucid_stored_list}
\alias{cellucid_stored_list}
\title{List what this browser keeps}
\usage{
cellucid_stored_list(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{bytes} (What the kept items and saved states take), \code{connection_speeds} (Hosts whose connection speed is remembered), \code{datasets} (Most recently used first), \code{decoder_choices} (Decoder choices measured in this browser), \code{my_datasets} (The datasets opened in this browser (datasets_list lists each) and the files of this computer among them it can reopen), \code{room} (What the browser says of the site's storage), \code{saved_states} (The histories kept in this browser (history_saved_list lists each)). Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
Everything kept in this browser for later visits, as the Stored dialog lists it: per dataset (its file's name and host) the converted copies, downloads, downloaded parts and gene indexes with their sizes; then the saved states, My datasets, the connection speeds and the decoder choices; and how much room the browser gives the site.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{stored.list} (Stored). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_stored_list(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
